Start with HTML:
```html
<button id="saveButton">Save</button>
<p id="status">Not saved</p>
```

Add CSS for presentation:
```css
button {
  border-radius: 8px;
  padding: 8px;
}
```

Add JavaScript for behavior:
```js
document.querySelector("#saveButton").addEventListener("click", () => {
  document.querySelector("#status").textContent = "Saved";
});
```

Three small pieces are doing the work:
- `querySelector` finds the element.
- `addEventListener` waits for the click.
- `textContent` changes the text.
